// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-units-oracle.py --gopp %gopp --out %t --seeds 3 --j1 | FileCheck %s
// P03.25 (GEN-14, R10, owner decision 2026-10-30): generic unit code computes
// what plain code computes. Random programs of unit-generic functions
// (products and quotients of their values and unit literals, calls of other
// generics with unit arguments made of their parameters) are checked by gopp
// (no error) and every value at every instance that main reaches is
// evaluated twice with exact rationals: as plain code with the real units
// (EXP-33), and as the generic code runs once for all instances with the
// collapse sites that gopp records (`unit-site`); the quantities must agree.
// A small sample here; more seeds with 1 and 8 body threads:
// units-generic-oracle.long, longer chains: units-generic-oracle-deep.long.
// CHECK: oracle: 3 programs, {{[0-9]+}} instances, 0 mismatches
